223-80","when":"November 1995","p":29,"h":null},{"id":"B225-63","when":"February 1997","p":20,"h":null},{"id":"B230-05","when":"June 2003","p":3,"h":"Contents"},{"id":"B230-06","when":"June 2003","p":3,"h":"Officers and contributors"},{"id":"B235-10","when":"September 2005","p":5,"h":"George French Trophy"}],"photos":[{"f":"crops/B147/B147-p14-tony-fairclough.jpg","c":"CENTRE Tony Fairclough","id":"B147-25","w":"May 1962"},{"f":"crops/B150/B150-p23-fairclough-inter-counties.jpg","c":"Tony Fairclough (Surrey) leads M. Dixon (Herts.) and G. Cooper (Derbys.) in the Junior Inter-County race, where he finished 16th.","id":"B150-39","w":"May 1963"},{"f":"crops/B153/B153-p01-tony-fairclough-cover.jpg","c":"FRONT COVER: (Ed. Lacey) Tony Fairclough, one of Britain's leading juniors, fights his way past Graham (Windsor) in the Southern championships to finish 3rd. Two weeks later he was 5th in the 'National'.","id":"B153-01","w":"April 1964"},{"f":"crops/B154/B154-p19-club-3-miles-montage.jpg","c":"THE CLUB '3' (Top, l.to r.) John Bicourt 8th; The start; Jack Brown leads Mike Shingles. (Bottom l.to r.) John Moore 7th, Tony Fairclough 3rd, Laurie O'Hara 2nd, Gerry North 1st (Photos:C. Shippen.)","id":"B154-44","w":"November 1964"},{"f":"crops/B158/B158-p01-fairclough-ohara-macher-shield.jpg","c":"Every inch counts, even after 10 miles slogging across country on a murky January afternoon. Tony Fairclough and Laurie O'Hara fight out the right to hold the \"Macher Shield\" for 1966 in a thrilling finish. Tony (41) was the winner.","id":"B158-01","w":"March 1966"},{"f":"crops/B161/B161-p01-tony-fairclough-cover.jpg","c":"FRONT COVER (R. Linstead)--Tony Fairclough, first Belgravian to finish in the National at Norwich, sets the pace for D. Holt (Hercules) and R. Moore (Longwood).","id":"B161-01","w":"March 1967"},{"f":"crops/B161/B161-p20-club-10-miles-hart-fairclough-kerr-walker.jpg","c":"LEFT: Hart leads Fairclough in the chase for O'Hara. RIGHT: Bill Kerr paces \"World Sports\" star Charlie Walker!","id":"B161-29","w":"March 1967"},{"f":"crops/B170/B170-p08-fairclough-major-changeover.jpg","c":"LEFT: Tony Fairclough completes our fastest short stage to send Adrian Major away.","id":"B170-11","w":"June 1969"},{"f":"crops/B171/B171-p32-fairclough-ohara-piotrowski.jpg","c":"Fairclough, O'Hara and Piotrowski are all set for some fast road times","id":"B171-57","w":"September 1969"},{"f":"crops/B177/B177-p16-road-race-runners.jpg","c":"The 5¾-miles championship field, still hunched after one mile. Front row: Pat O'Connor (12), Tony Fairclough (21), Peter Carton (19), Trevor Hart (23), and Lionel Mann (9). The three framed heads look like those of Chris Steer, John Thresher and Dereck Fernee.","id":"B177-34","w":"June 1971"},{"f":"crops/B180/B180-p27-tony-fairclough.jpg","c":"Top left: It's pleasing to see Tony Fairclough back in action recently and not doing too badly either.","id":"B180-47","w":"March 1973"},{"f":"crops/B184/B184-p19-surrey-county-trio.jpg","c":"The Belgrave trio of John Stow (27), Colin Pearson (24) and Tony Fairclough (18) plough their way through the Surrey County Cross County Championship and help take the team to 2nd place.","id":"B184-52","w":"March 1974"},{"f":"crops/B199/B199-p41-baton-changes.jpg","c":"Some interesting styles in baton changing at the 100 x 1 mile relay.\nTop left. Kevin Clarke (83) demonstrates the cross leg shuffle as he takes the baton from new member L.Lyons.\nTop right. M.Harrison (13) demonstrates the walkers change as he hands over to P.Moysey.\nBottom left. Steve Webb (69) milkman to the last gives Pat Lyttle no change.\nCentre. Ian Morton (75) provides a fine example of the jumping high level pass with Graham Allerton intercepting.\nBottom right. Colin Pearson (84) uses the jumping low level pass to send Tony Fairclough on his way.","id":"B199-109","w":"October 1979"},{"f":"crops/B205/B205-p31-club-5000m.jpg","c":"Still bunched in the Club 5000m Championship. Ley Coy leads from Laurie O'Hara and Tony Binda followed by; Tony Fairclough,Simon Williamson,Leo Lyons(hidden),Martin Head(94),Bill Downey(95) and Tony Grant(40)","id":"B205-60","w":"October 1982"},{"f":"crops/B230/B230-p09-southern-junior-1963.jpg","c":"Right: Tony runs to 18th place in the Southern Junior CC Champs of 1963.","id":"B230-19","w":"June 2003"},{"f":"crops/B246/B246-p01-belles-sutton.jpg","c":"Above: At the home UKWAL match at Sutton the Belles just missed stretching their win streak to cover two complete seasons.  Another four match points would have done it – but they don’t seem too downhearted as they now look forward to 2007 and UKWAL Division Two.\n\nFrom left to right – standing: Juliet Fielden, Katryna Euridge, Eva Massey, John Vernon, Sarah Gailey, Jayne Anderson, Chris Privett, Claire Robinson, Bob Bridges (Joint Team Manager), Cynthia James (Joint Team Manager), Rex Bale, Carl Lawton, Jennifer Culley, Tony Fairclough, Sarah Murphy, Derek Jones, Ray James. Kneeling: Sarah Wellstead, Janine Whitlock, Gail Porter, Dian Holden, Hazel Mead.","id":"B246-02","w":"September 2006"},{"f":"crops/B223/B223-p29-track-judges.jpg","c":"Right: Track Judges Tony Fairclough, Natalie Stracey and Pat Mead are regaled with another amusing anecdote from Stuart Bennett (seated), or is he making some caustic comment about the timekeeper in unaccustomed shades - Cecil Gittins","id":"B223-80","w":"November 1995"},{"f":"crops/B235/B235-p05-george-french-trophy.jpg","c":"","id":"B235-10","w":"September 2005"}],"photo":{"file":"crops/B147/B147-p14-tony-fairclough.jpg","caption":"CENTRE Tony Fairclough","source":"B147-25","when":"May 1962"},"slarchive":"https://slarchive.org/#athlete/tony-fairclough","slRaces":22,"x":1,"legend":false}